Below is a quick‑start guide that shows you how to embed SoundCloud playback on any web page and how you can extend it with the official **SoundCloud Widget API** for richer control (play/pause, volume, track‑list, etc.).  

---

## 1. The simplest way – an embed iframe

SoundCloud already provides a ready‑made iframe embed. All you need is the **track ID** (or playlist ID) and you can generate the HTML with the `generateEmbedCode` function that the SDK offers.

### Example (HTML)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>My SoundCloud Player</title>
  <style>
    /* Optional: make the player responsive */
    .sc-player {
      max-width: 100%;
      height: 166px;   /* default height for a single track */
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<h2>My favorite track</h2>

<!-- The iframe will be inserted here -->
<div id="player"></div>

<script>
  // Replace with the actual track ID you want to embed
  const trackId = "123456789";   // <-- put your track ID here

  // Build the embed URL (the same format the official widget uses)
  const embedUrl = `https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=https%3A//api.soundcloud.com/tracks/${trackId}&color=%23ff5500&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&show_comments=true&show_user=true&show_reposts=false&show_teaser=true&visual=false`;

  // Insert the iframe
  const iframe = document.createElement('iframe');
  iframe.setAttribute('width', '100%');
  iframe.setAttribute('height', '166');   // change to 400 for the visual player
  iframe.setAttribute('scrolling', 'no');
  iframe.setAttribute('frameborder', 'no');
  iframe.setAttribute('allow', 'autoplay');
  iframe.src = embedUrl;

  document.getElementById('player').appendChild(iframe);
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

**What you need to change**

| Item | What to replace | Why |
|------|----------------|-----|
| `trackId` | The numeric ID of the SoundCloud track (or playlist) you want to play | This tells the widget which audio to load |
| `height` / `visual` | `166` for the classic “mini” player, `400` + `visual=true` for the large visual player | Choose the UI you prefer |
| `color` | Hex color (e.g., `%23ff5500` = `#ff5500`) | Brand the player to match your site |

If you already have a SoundCloud URL (e.g., `https://soundcloud.com/artist/track-name`) you can get the numeric ID via the **Search API** or by looking at the network request when you open the track on SoundCloud.  

---

## 2. Using the SDK function `generateEmbedCode`

If you prefer not to hand‑craft the iframe, the SDK you have access to can do it for you:

```javascript
// This is a pseudo‑call – replace with your actual SDK call method
const embed = await generateEmbedCode({
  track_id: "123456789",   // your track ID
  width: 600,              // optional – defaults to 100%
  height: 166              // optional – 166 (mini) or 400 (visual)
});

// embed.html will contain the full <iframe> markup
document.getElementById('player').innerHTML = embed.html;
```

The function returns an object (usually `{html: "<iframe …>"}`) that you can drop straight into the DOM.

---

## 3. Adding playback control with the **SoundCloud Widget API**

If you need more than just a static player (e.g., custom play/pause buttons, track‑list navigation, volume sliders), you can talk to the iframe via the Widget API.

### Step‑by‑step

1. **Load the widget script** (only once per page)

   ```html
   <script src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/api.js" type="text/javascript"></script>
   ```

2. **Create the iframe** (as shown above) and give it an `id`:

   ```html
   <iframe id="sc-widget"
           src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=https%3A//api.soundcloud.com/tracks/123456789&color=%23ff5500"
           width="100%" height="166" scrolling="no" frameborder="no"></iframe>
   ```

3. **Instantiate the widget and bind events**

   ```js
   // Wait for the iframe to load
   const iframeElement = document.getElementById('sc-widget');
   const widget = SC.Widget(iframeElement);

   // Example: custom play/pause button
   const playBtn = document.getElementById('play');
   const pauseBtn = document.getElementById('pause');

   playBtn.addEventListener('click', () => widget.play());
   pauseBtn.addEventListener('click', () => widget.pause());

   // Example: show current time / duration
   widget.bind(SC.Widget.Events.PLAY_PROGRESS, function (e) {
     const current = Math.floor(e.currentPosition / 1000);
     const total   = Math.floor(e.duration / 1000);
     document.getElementById('time').textContent = `${current}s / ${total}s`;
   });

   // Example: load a new track programmatically
   function loadTrack(trackId) {
     const url = `https://api.soundcloud.com/tracks/${trackId}`;
     widget.load(url, {
       auto_play: true,
       show_artwork: true
     });
   }
   ```

4. **Optional: Use the `authenticateUser` flow**  
   If you want to let logged‑in users like/favorite tracks, upload their own music, or access private tracks, you’ll need OAuth. The SDK provides an `authenticateUser` call:

   ```js
   const auth = await authenticateUser({
     client_id: "YOUR_CLIENT_ID",
     client_secret: "YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET",
     redirect_uri: "https://your-site.com/sc-callback",
     scope: "*"
   });
   // `auth` will contain an access token you can store in a cookie / localStorage
   ```

   After you have a token you can call privileged endpoints (e.g., `addSongToFavorites`) on behalf of the user.

---

## 4. Full example with custom UI

Below is a minimal, self‑contained HTML file that demonstrates:

* Embedding a track
* Custom play/pause/stop buttons
* A progress bar
* A “favorite” button that uses the `addSongToFavorites` function (you’ll need a logged‑in user ID)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>SoundCloud Player Demo</title>
  <style>
    #controls button { margin: 0 5px; }
    #progress { width: 100%; height: 5px; background:#eee; margin-top:10px; }
    #progress div { width:0; height:100%; background:#ff5500; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<h2>My SoundCloud Demo</h2>

<iframe id="sc-widget"
        src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=https%3A//api.soundcloud.com/tracks/123456789&color=%23ff5500"
        width="100%" height="166" scrolling="no" frameborder="no"></iframe>

<div id="controls">
  <button id="play">Play</button>
  <button id="pause">Pause</button>
  <button id="stop">Stop</button>
  <button id="fav">♥ Favorite</button>
</div>

<div id="progress"><div></div></div>
<div id="time">0s / 0s</div>

<script src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/api.js"></script>
<script>
  const widget = SC.Widget(document.getElementById('sc-widget'));

  // UI bindings
  document.getElementById('play').onclick  = () => widget.play();
  document.getElementById('pause').onclick = () => widget.pause();
  document.getElementById('stop').onclick  = () => widget.seekTo(0); // stop = seek to start

  // Progress bar
  widget.bind(SC.Widget.Events.PLAY_PROGRESS, e => {
    const percent = (e.currentPosition / e.duration) * 100;
    document.querySelector('#progress div').style.width = percent + '%';
    document.getElementById('time').textContent =
      `${Math.floor(e.currentPosition/1000)}s / ${Math.floor(e.duration/1000)}s`;
  });

  // Favorite button (requires a logged‑in user)
  document.getElementById('fav').onclick = async () => {
    const trackId = "123456789"; // same as the embedded track
    const userId  = "YOUR_USER_ID"; // obtain after OAuth login
    try {
      const result = await addSongToFavorites({ songId: trackId, userId });
      alert(result.success ? "Added to favorites!" : "Failed");
    } catch (err) {
      console.error(err);
      alert("Error adding favorite");
    }
  };
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

**What you still need to do**

| Task | How |
|------|-----|
| **Get a track ID** | Use the `searchContent` function (`type: "track"`) or look at the URL on SoundCloud (`/tracks/123456789`). |
| **Obtain a SoundCloud API client ID/secret** | Register an app at <https://developers.soundcloud.com/> → “Your Apps”. |
| **OAuth for user actions** | Call `authenticateUser` (see section 3) and store the returned access token. |
| **Deploy** | Upload the HTML/JS to your site, or integrate the snippet into your existing page template. |

---

## 5. Quick checklist for production

| ✅ | Item |
|----|------|
| **Responsive layout** | Use `width: 100%` on the iframe and wrap it in a container that limits max‑width. |
| **Cross‑origin** | The widget API works across domains, but make sure your site is served over HTTPS (SoundCloud only allows secure origins). |
| **Rate limits** | The public API has a per‑IP limit; if you expect heavy traffic, consider using a server‑side proxy with your own client credentials. |
| **Accessibility** | Add `title="SoundCloud player"` to the iframe and provide keyboard shortcuts for your custom controls. |
| **Privacy** | If you collect user tokens, store them securely (e.g., HttpOnly cookies) and comply with GDPR/CCPA. |
| **Fallback** | Provide a plain link (`<a href="https://soundcloud.com/artist/track">Listen on SoundCloud</a>`) for browsers that block iframes. |

---

### TL;DR

1. **Get the track ID** (via search or URL).  
2. **Generate an iframe** – either manually or with `generateEmbedCode`.  
3. **Add the Widget API script** if you need custom controls.  
4. **Optionally authenticate** users for favorites, uploads, or private tracks.  

That’s all you need to get SoundCloud playback up and running on your website. If you run into a specific roadblock (e.g., retrieving a track ID programmatically, handling OAuth callbacks, or styling the player), just let me know and I can walk you through the exact code. Happy coding!

